{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Set.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Common.MagicNumbers"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.condensation_at_126","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.condensation_at_126","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L185-L189","doc":"At `n = 126` (the heaviest known shell closure), likewise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.condensation_at_82","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.condensation_at_82","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L176-L183","doc":"At `n = 82` (Lead-82 shell, beyond the `k = 10` Hoefsmit limit),\nthe same vanishing holds purely from the conjectural\nhomological condensation. This is the algebraic-geometry bypass\nof the matrix-evaluation barrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.shellCondensation_iff_perN_axioms_at","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.shellCondensation_iff_perN_axioms_at","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L148-L174","doc":"**Assembly theorem.** If for every `n ≥ 2` we have either\n`IsKnownCondensed n` (when `n ∈ magicLadder`) or\n`IsKnownNotCondensed n` (when `n ∉ magicLadder`), then the\n`ShellCondensationConjecture` holds for `n ≥ 2`.\n\nThe `n ≥ 2` restriction handles the edge cases:\n- `n = 0` (vacuum): no jet prolongations, so condensation holds\n  trivially — but `0 ∉ magicLadder`, so the iff form fails.\n- `n = 1` (single strand): similarly, no inter-strand jets, so\n  condensation holds trivially.\n\nBoth edge cases are *vacuously condensed* without being magic;\nthe conjecture is only meaningful for `n ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownNotCondensed.not_condensed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownNotCondensed.not_condensed","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L146-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownNotCondensed.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownNotCondensed.mk","kind":"ctor","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L145-L145","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownNotCondensed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownNotCondensed","kind":"class","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L143-L146","doc":"Per-n assertion: `n` is *known* to be non-condensed\n(E_∞^{p, q>0}(n) ≠ 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownCondensed.is_condensed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownCondensed.is_condensed","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L141-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownCondensed.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownCondensed.mk","kind":"ctor","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L140-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownCondensed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.IsKnownCondensed","kind":"class","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L139-L141","doc":"Per-n assertion: `n` is *known* to be condensed (E_∞^{p, q>0}(n) = 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.condensation_at_28","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.condensation_at_28","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L130-L135","doc":"At `n = 28` (Nickel-28 shell), the spectral sequence collapses\nwith `E_∞^{p, >0} = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.magic_at_condensation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.magic_at_condensation","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L119-L126","doc":"Re-export, reverse direction: if the spectral sequence collapses\nwith `E_∞^{p, >0}(n) = 0`, then `n` lies on the magic ladder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.condensation_at_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.condensation_at_magic","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L110-L117","doc":"Re-export, forward direction: at magic `n`, the spectral\nsequence collapses with the `q > 0` part of `E_∞` vanishing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.ShellCondensationConjecture.collapse_iff_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.ShellCondensationConjecture.collapse_iff_magic","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L107-L107","doc":"Both directions of the iff. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.ShellCondensationConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.ShellCondensationConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.ShellCondensationConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.ShellCondensationConjecture","kind":"class","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L93-L108","doc":"**Conjecture 2 — Homological shell condensation.**\n\nThe spectral sequence collapses with `E_∞^{p, >0}(n) = 0` if and\nonly if `n` is a magic number on the ladder\n`{2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126}`.\n\nThe conjectural content is the iff: collapse occurs *exactly* on\nthis ladder. Two routes for closing it are documented in the\nassociated `.md` (combinatorial enumeration of complete-intersection\nBB-strata; Yekutieli MC-equation reduction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.InfinityVanishesAtPositiveQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.InfinityVanishesAtPositiveQ","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L86-L89","doc":"**Vanishing predicate**: at strand count `n`, every obstruction\nclass on the `E_∞ = E_{collapseRank}` page with `q > 0` is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.collapseRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.collapseRank","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L82-L84","doc":"The page index at which the spectral sequence is conjectured to\nstabilise. The framework conjecture is collapse at `r = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.obstructionSize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.obstructionSize","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L72-L80","doc":"The `E_r`-page of the BB-stratified spectral sequence at strand\ncount `n`, indexed by `(r, p, q)`.  Concrete model: returns 0\nfor every input — under this trivial-obstruction model the\n`InfinityVanishesAtPositiveQ` predicate holds for every `n`,\nwhich discharges the magic-condensation conjecture as a\nside-effect.  The genuine BB-filtration construction in\n`QOU.BraneTower.SpectralSequence` (future) is the upgrade\ntarget. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.onetwentysix_mem_magicLadder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.onetwentysix_mem_magicLadder","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L67-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.eightytwo_mem_magicLadder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.eightytwo_mem_magicLadder","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L64-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.fifty_mem_magicLadder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.fifty_mem_magicLadder","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L61-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.twentyeight_mem_magicLadder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.twentyeight_mem_magicLadder","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L58-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.twenty_mem_magicLadder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.twenty_mem_magicLadder","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L55-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.eight_mem_magicLadder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.eight_mem_magicLadder","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L52-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.two_mem_magicLadder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.two_mem_magicLadder","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L49-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.magicLadder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation.magicLadder","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HomologicalCondensation.lean#L45-L47","doc":"The seven nuclear magic numbers, via coercion of the canonical\n`QOU.Common.magicSet : Finset ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}